  ssp1_policy.xml — SSP1-1.9 Sustainability (1.5 °C pathway)
  ===========================================================
  Narrative: rapid global cooperation, low resource intensity, strong
  climate governance. Strict near-term carbon pricing forces deep
  decarbonisation by 2035–2040. High renewable mandate throughout.

  Project links:
    Rail_EU_DEV signals Europe's high institutional capacity and policy
    ambition. Hospital Proj_003 and Proj_001 reflect social investment
    consistent with SSP1's human-development focus. Hydro retrofits are
    deployed early and fully.

  Carbon prices [$/tonne CO2]:
    Africa: 80→500 (just-transition pathway with high near-term budget
            allowing development while tightening steeply post-2030)
    Asia:   65→400
    Europe: 120→800 (consistent with Rail_EU_DEV institutional capacity)
    LATAM:  80→400
    (All priced per region; regional markets reflect domestic policy capacity)

  Renewable electricity standard (minimum fraction from renewables):
    Africa: 36%→98% (2020→2050)
    Asia:   26%→97%
    Europe: 44%→99%
    LATAM:  52%→99%
-->
